  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.0: first complete stable release. API settlement with no compatibility aliases: the consumer method Execute is now OnActive, Step is now Advance, and the typed Apply/Advance overloads live on the Timeline pair surface (the Lane facade is removed). Playback floors receipted on every host shape and CPU tier: shared-clock crowds 0.08 ns/row, per-entity calls 0.80 ns forward, non-AVX2 tiers 0.48 ns via the kernel tier ladder and flat record arena, bit-exact across AVX2, Vector128, and scalar. Bakes dispatch by discovered signature through the IBake marker; the live playground handles arbitrary valid authoring. Pair-typed folding is pair-isolated: Timeline<TTrack,TClip> measures and plays only its own pair, never another pair's consumers. OnActive with no gameplay parameters registers a dispatch-only consumer, fired per row at the position's tick by the no-output Apply(indices, positions, forward) overload.",
